==Trivia==
*Chalkboard Punk Cat is a reference to Masami Iwaki from ''[[wikipedia:Dokaben|Dokaben]]'', who is typically seen with an identical-looking ''[[wikipedia:School uniforms in Japan#Gakuran|gakuran]]'' cap and a two-leaved twig in his mouth.
*Chalkboard Eraser Cat's Japanese name, Nekokubankeshi, is a portmanteau of ''neko'' (cat) and ''kokubankeshi'' (chalkboard eraser); while Chalkboard Punk Cat's, Nekokubanchō, combines that with ''banchō'' (leader of a group of juvenile delinquents, or in recent times a title of honor for people with leadership personalities).

